Leaves the keys of hardware keyboards on iOS, iPadOS, Mac Catalyst and tvOS to GameController, through which the engine reads every key with its release, so SDL turns only the presses of remotes and game controllers into keys, whether a keyboard is connected or not, and hands UIKit the presses whose key the app drops through its event filter, such as the Menu press of the Apple TV remote while the app leaves the back button to the system. It also stops turning arrows and escape into key commands, and the swipes of the Apple TV remote into arrows, which the engine reads as the stick of the remote, and reads the Siri Remote that the joystick subsystem opens only where SDL builds that subsystem.

